Likewise in the other intermediate directions are priyaka trees on all sides;
this is celebrated as the dwelling city of Śyāmā.

The daily service of the venerable Devī could not be performed by the Mantriṇī [from so far away];
therefore, a mansion was also constructed near the Cintāmaṇi palace
for that venerable mistress of mantras by Tvaṣṭṛ, the artisan of the gods, and by Maya.

3.32.m:
Agastya said:
There must surely be guardians of the seven ramparts of iron and the other metals;
proclaim their names, O wise one, so that my doubt may be dispelled.
